#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:66
#: ec82cb2ec0fc439e9899d5692006d6dd
msgid "Second OSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:68
#: bd7fcb806f3e42ab854f82a8d26a0f51
msgid "ArduPilot now supports having two OSD backends simultaneously. For example, this would be used on long range planes where a shorter range HD system like DJI or Walksnail would be used up until it reached the limit of its range, and then the pilot would switch to using an analog, lower definition, longer range system while operating at distance. In fact, it is possible to have three OSD systems running simultaneously since pure MSP OSD telemetry is active if any ONE OSD backend is running and an MSP base OSD could be attached to a serial port using MSP protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:70
#: 78cd26cd922c456580b679ae8f1038d0
msgid "A typical configuration would be to use the onboard analog video OSD system, together with a DisplayPort system. The setup would be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:72
#: ca3fd42571974f04a6d2ace403fd5262
msgid ":ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` = 1 to enable the analog system, with a long range video transmitter connected to the Video output pin of the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:73
#: 01dd994748374a1bae24d24577ef21b2
msgid ":ref:`OSD_TYPE2<OSD_TYPE2>` = 5 to enable the second DisplayPort backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:74
#: e421a4890a064936bc7cff13eb0f31d8
msgid "``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 42 for the serial port which the DJI or Walksnail VTX is connected for telemetry input to the goggles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:76
#: 0d24537c04304ae5a8f4a9b47e4add1e
msgid "there are several combinations of first and second OSD type that are not allowed and will result in a pre-arm warning to change configuration. The most obvious is using two osd types of the same kind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:78
#: b692d3b04655428a9f560706f8baa29c
msgid "although both OSD systems work simultaneously, if the two OSD systems are different resolutions, you will need to setup multiple OSD screens (see below) and switch the screen layout when switching to using the different system (ie when  swapping the video display being actively used). It is possible to create a single screen layout that works for both, but the advantage of the HD system would be obviously reduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:80
#: dadb955ef60a46dcb40f80c3133d78be
msgid "screen item setup for HD displays may give warnings in Mission Planner about screen location parameters being out of range. Just ignore those."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:85
#: afba9d72d61d4ea6b5595862ab2f8923
msgid "Screens and screen switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:87
#: 77c403d6a0614aa984fb01cc8c2d1340
msgid "For multiple screen layouts, each parameter's \"OSD\" part is trailed by a number, starting with \"1\" for the screen number for which the parameter applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:89
#: 05337304d3ac458383fc76c5c0d41335
msgid "``OSDn_<ITEM>_<PARAMETER>`` - n represents the screen number, ITEM the displayed data item, and PARAMETER, the enable and positions parameters for this display item. OSD settings default to allowing up to 4 screens available, each optionally enabled. Displayed data items can be shown on one screen and not on others by setting its ENABLE parameter for that screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:91
#: 2cd09be2b9174e00a0f7380877c773ce
msgid "Set parameters ``OSDn_CHAN_MIN`` and ``OSDn_CHAN_MAX`` are used to adjust RC channel pwm limits to use for switching to a respective screen. Be careful not to have overlapping PWM ranges for two screens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:93
#: cde7fd8990774415b8b28193b23fe0bb
msgid "There are different switch-method options to meet individual RC systems switch layout requirements. These can be set by parameter: :ref:`OSD_SW_METHOD<OSD_SW_METHOD>`. The options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:97
#: a4a3d5b8128b4f60a0e9fca60919256b
msgid "0 = switches to next screen if the set RC channel's (:ref:`OSD_CHAN<OSD_CHAN>`) value is changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:98
#: be279445bb5a4474a74efecb01518efb
msgid "1 = directly selects a screen based on the set pwm limits for each respective screen. RC channel value must change for new pwm value to be recognized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:99
#: 872f53f8d34d43cd83642a6d20ad4513
msgid "2 = toggles screens on a low to high transition of set RC channel. keeps toggling to next screen every 1s while channel value is kept high"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:104
#: 927f0364555842c48666b8bbbedf5a0c
msgid "Panel items"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:106
#: 66f7fcc9a41d4cb2800e01c7b612b5b1
msgid "Each OSD panel item uses a set of three variables to be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:108
#: c15e0275084e4269b1b4f729d57ac062
msgid "``OSDn_<ITEM>EN`` - activates the respective item when set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:109
#: df781a5b1ce84247982837d7b7b3d298
msgid "``OSDn_<ITEM>_X`` and ``OSDn_<ITEM>_Y`` set the horizontal and vertical position of the item, starting with ``X = 0`` and ``Y = 0`` in the upper left corner of your screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:113
#: 8325ba3ad9a8453eb6245dbec1f236c7
msgid "The typical MAXChip based OSD screen has a visible matrix of 30 horizontal x 13 vertical chars in NTSC standard, while PAL standard has 16 vertical chars. The OSD code enables auto-detection of NTSC vs. PAL to match input signal properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:115
#: bb6195bea6a84cac8cdddf22351bcfca
msgid "ArduPilot calculates an sensor-less airspeed estimate that is used if no sensor is present or fails. :ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>` must be set to zero in order to display this value as the airspeed item, if no sensor is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:118
#: 1097c516cdef4ed2b31f3e93f27fb6df
msgid "Displaying statistics on a dedicated screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:119
#: 6950b6ceb2f64de9b3cf5beba3651ffc
msgid "Displaying statistics on a dedicated screen requires enabling at least one extra screen by setting the respective ``OSDn_ENABLE`` to 1. By default, ArduPilot has only one screen active so in a typical setup one would set (:ref:`OSD2_ENABLE<OSD2_ENABLE>`) = 1 and then enabling the OSD stats panel on screen 2 by setting (:ref:`OSD2_STATS_EN<OSD2_STATS_EN>`) = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:122
#: 2443f381fd9b43cf9775a8349faefae0
msgid "When the OSD switches to this screen it will check the value of the :ref:`OSD2_STATS_EN<OSD2_STATS_EN>` parameter and if enabled it will override the default behavior of the following OSD items:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:124
#: 7c955671e13a48bf90e17facf60044c8
msgid "OSDn_MESSAGE will display STATS followed by flight time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:125
#: 41bf5c1cf98243e39a031b2fd75f2e76
msgid "OSDn_ALTITUDE will display max altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:126
#: 942e6ff4f69f4651a8e8e90176f4654b
msgid "OSDn_BAT_VOLT will display min voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:127
#: b6b65c84027f4568badf8fc2aacfea8b
msgid "OSDn_CURRENT will display max current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:128
#: 0e78951a5512424b800ca2566716de05
msgid "OSDn_GSPEED will display max ground speed (or airspeed if ``OSDn_ASPEED_EN`` is set to 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:129
#: f9df3d092f374c02a04c9d39ef37e192
msgid "OSDn_HOMEDIST will alternates max distance from home and total traveled distance every 2 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:130
#: f908e1fa741642a19a166d195b517378
msgid "OSDn_RSSI will display min rssi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:134
#: 7eee84acf8384f9ebd2b2497b5935926
msgid "Callsign panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:136
#: b0260333426447b2a974a8a4238fc202
msgid "This panel allows to display your amateur radio callsign (or any other individual character string) on your onboard OSD screen. It will read the character string from a file named \"callsign.txt\" placed in the root of your SD card. Mind that the default ardupilot charsets require to use capital letters for correct display. Using MAVftp is a convenient option to upload the file to your SD card without having to physically remove it from your flightcontroller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:139
#: 7a729afbd0834137ba09a53af547a58e
msgid "User Programmable Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:140
#: 3a4fafc71fba4a7184de26f866faeea3
msgid "Several user defined warnings can be set which will flash the respective osd panel item when warning level is reached or exceeded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:142
#: a058265e1be6422bba6d831145810111
msgid ":ref:`OSD_W_BATVOLT<OSD_W_BATVOLT>` - Blinks battery voltage panel if less than this value. 0-100V with up tenth volt precision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-osd-overview.rst:143
#: 178f906a1cfd4067b90f9026479671a0
